1
00:00:00,169 --> 00:00:02,054
Sync and corrections by n17t01
www.addic7ed.com

2
00:00:02,220 --> 00:00:03,667
(Crows cawing)

3
00:00:04,731 --> 00:00:05,779
<i>(Frankie) Halloween--</i>

4
00:00:05,898 --> 00:00:07,460
<i>the most terrifying time</i>
<i>of the year,</i>

5
00:00:07,565 --> 00:00:10,198
<i>where frightening horrors</i>
<i>lurk around every corner.</i>

6
00:00:10,579 --> 00:00:12,191
I got my learners permit!

7
00:00:12,343 --> 00:00:13,823
Aah!

8
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:16,847
I'm 18!
I get to pick the president!

9
00:00:16,979 --> 00:00:18,281
Aah!

10
00:00:18,426 --> 00:00:20,356
I signed you up
to work at the Halloween fair.

11
00:00:20,452 --> 00:00:22,576
Aah!

12
00:00:22,922 --> 00:00:26,206
Brick, why would you
volunteer me at school?

13
00:00:26,310 --> 00:00:29,153
You know the line--
"sorry, my mom works long hours.

14
00:00:29,273 --> 00:00:31,577
We hardly ever see her."
I made you memorize it.

15
00:00:31,691 --> 00:00:34,022
Well, I thought it was okay since
you're not working now. (Door opens)

16
00:00:34,174 --> 00:00:36,041
You didn't tell people that, did you?
(Door closes)

17
00:00:36,161 --> 00:00:37,575
(Sighs) If they know
I'm not working,

18
00:00:37,673 --> 00:00:38,942
I'm gonna get calls
for everything.

19
00:00:39,059 --> 00:00:41,074
Mike, do not answer the phone.

20
00:00:41,202 --> 00:00:42,004
Never do.

21
00:00:42,135 --> 00:00:43,553
(Sue) Maintaining safe speed.

22
00:00:43,684 --> 00:00:45,817
(Gasps) Uh-oh.
Obstruction in the road.

23
00:00:45,956 --> 00:00:48,507
Checking mirrors.
Applying brake.

24
00:00:48,634 --> 00:00:49,616
Beep!

25
00:00:52,988 --> 00:00:54,427
Checking mirrors.

26
00:00:54,580 --> 00:00:56,016
Re-entering traffic.

27
00:00:56,134 --> 00:00:57,599
Enough practicing, Sue!

28
00:00:57,724 --> 00:00:59,412
You're gonna have to learn
to drive a real car.

29
00:00:59,509 --> 00:01:00,568
I'm not
driving you around forever

30
00:01:00,671 --> 00:01:02,211
listening to one direction.

31
00:01:02,321 --> 00:01:03,738
I'm starting to <i>like</i>
a couple of those songs.

32
00:01:03,862 --> 00:01:05,477
You guys...

33
00:01:07,574 --> 00:01:09,080
after my near-death experience

34
00:01:09,178 --> 00:01:10,867
accidentally driving
the Donahues' car,

35
00:01:11,034 --> 00:01:12,652
I am not getting
behind the wheel again

36
00:01:12,758 --> 00:01:15,822
until I feel completely prepared
for any situation.

37
00:01:15,990 --> 00:01:18,250
(Door closes)
Hey, Sue. Just a heads up,

38
00:01:18,377 --> 00:01:20,314
traffic in the family room
is horrible.

39
00:01:20,607 --> 00:01:21,525
Good tip.

40
00:01:21,695 --> 00:01:23,037
I'll take the hallway.

41
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:25,489
<i>(Man's voice moans
diabolically)</i> Hey, Brick,

42
00:01:25,645 --> 00:01:27,378
what's this I got
in the mail that you didn't?

43
00:01:27,516 --> 00:01:29,387
(Gasps) Oh!
It's a voter guide,

44
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:31,740
sent personally to me,
Axl Redford Heck,

45
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:33,567
signifying my readiness
to take my rightful place

46
00:01:33,683 --> 00:01:34,526
among the adult,

47
00:01:34,632 --> 00:01:36,298
president-choosing citizens
of our country.

48
00:01:36,625 --> 00:01:38,410
Do you even know
who you're voting for?

49
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:40,155
Not yet. I'll wait
till I hear 'em all sing,

50
00:01:40,283 --> 00:01:41,543
and then
I'll text in my choice.

51
00:01:41,684 --> 00:01:43,497
Good idea. Your vote
shouldn't count anyway.

52
00:01:46,821 --> 00:01:48,142
(Clinks)

53
00:01:48,831 --> 00:01:50,436
Eh, good enough.

54
00:01:52,629 --> 00:01:54,005
Hi, Frankie!

55
00:01:54,199 --> 00:01:57,123
I see a happy Halloween
in your future!

56
00:01:57,228 --> 00:01:58,939
Oh, Nancy, you look great!

57
00:01:59,061 --> 00:02:00,098
Oh, thanks.

58
00:02:00,241 --> 00:02:02,021
I saw it in a catalog,
sewed it myself,

59
00:02:02,155 --> 00:02:03,906
and saved 14 bucks.

60
00:02:04,199 --> 00:02:06,112
And you look...

61
00:02:06,429 --> 00:02:07,869
Well, I already got
halfway dressed,

62
00:02:08,004 --> 00:02:09,612
and I couldn't find
the rest of my costume,

63
00:02:09,721 --> 00:02:12,095
so, yep. I'm raggedy mouse.

64
00:02:12,253 --> 00:02:13,081
(Laughs) (Clinks)

65
00:02:13,179 --> 00:02:15,669
I think it's fantastic.
Very creative.

66
00:02:15,833 --> 00:02:17,192
(Girl) Thank you!

67
00:02:17,611 --> 00:02:20,660
You know, I cannot get it up
for Halloween this year.

68
00:02:20,781 --> 00:02:23,299
I think losing my job
and starting school--

69
00:02:23,449 --> 00:02:25,472
it just all feels
like too much.

70
00:02:25,607 --> 00:02:26,938
I'm supposed to take Brick
trick-or-treating.

71
00:02:27,049 --> 00:02:28,515
I just want to
open a box of wine

72
00:02:28,646 --> 00:02:30,092
and stay home.

73
00:02:30,226 --> 00:02:31,541
Oh, I'll take him for you.

74
00:02:31,739 --> 00:02:33,359
I'm taking
Dottie and Shelly already,

75
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:35,635
so it would be no trouble
to have Brick come along.

76
00:02:35,817 --> 00:02:37,865
Oh, really? I could
pawn him off on you?

77
00:02:37,991 --> 00:02:39,390
You don't think
that makes me a bad mom?

78
00:02:39,579 --> 00:02:42,312
I don't think <i>that</i> does, no.

79
00:02:44,624 --> 00:02:46,696
We're not exactly
moving a lot of fish here.

80
00:02:46,810 --> 00:02:48,545
What happens
to all the leftovers?

81
00:02:50,399 --> 00:02:51,398
I know times are tough,

82
00:02:51,528 --> 00:02:53,617
but I'm not eating goldfish
for dinner.

83
00:02:53,730 --> 00:02:56,823
Well, apparently, fish mom
gets to bring home the fish.

84
00:02:56,995 --> 00:02:58,674
Mm. Fish mom should take 'em
down the hall

85
00:02:58,796 --> 00:03:00,105
to porcelain pond.

86
00:03:00,254 --> 00:03:01,303
(Laughs)

87
00:03:01,926 --> 00:03:02,519
<i>(Crowd cheering on TV)</i>

88
00:03:02,618 --> 00:03:04,705
Check me out. Just read
this whole book, cover to cover.

89
00:03:04,904 --> 00:03:07,735
Wow. First "Cat In The Hat,"
and now this.

90
00:03:07,854 --> 00:03:09,150
Hey, you told me
to get informed.

91
00:03:09,273 --> 00:03:11,826
But this is, like, way harder
than I thought it was gonna be.

92
00:03:11,953 --> 00:03:14,460
Seriously, sheriff?
(Chuckles) How do you pick?

93
00:03:14,592 --> 00:03:17,320
I like this guy 'cause
he's serious about crime.

94
00:03:17,499 --> 00:03:20,201
But then this other guy's
gonna get tough on crime.

95
00:03:20,325 --> 00:03:21,746
(Inhales sharply,
blows raspberry)

96
00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:23,406
What sheriff
are you guys gonna vote for?

97
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:26,466
Uh, we haven't really
made up our minds yet.

98
00:03:26,599 --> 00:03:27,777
What about the city council?

99
00:03:27,942 --> 00:03:30,573
You liking Paul Delvecchio
or Jennifer Farley?

100
00:03:31,295 --> 00:03:33,473
Yeah, I'm leaning
toward Delvecchio.

101
00:03:33,605 --> 00:03:35,005
Oh, are you?
Are you really?

102
00:03:35,124 --> 00:03:36,690
'Cause they're both people
from Jersey Shore.

103
00:03:36,817 --> 00:03:38,352
You guys haven't even
looked at this, have you?

104
00:03:39,278 --> 00:03:42,067
Okay, so maybe we don't always
vote for the little offices,

105
00:03:42,196 --> 00:03:45,016
but we vote for the big guys,
like president.

106
00:03:45,204 --> 00:03:46,546
You know,
maybe it's a good thing

107
00:03:46,679 --> 00:03:48,852
that he's studying up
on the sheriffs.

108
00:03:48,968 --> 00:03:50,097
He's never gonna
meet a president,

109
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:53,744
but I bet money you're gonna
run into a sheriff some day.

110
00:03:54,251 --> 00:03:56,235
Might want to take a look
at those judges, too.

111
00:03:56,752 --> 00:03:58,569
You two are what's wrong
with America.

112
00:03:59,243 --> 00:04:00,217
(Both exhale)

113
00:04:01,238 --> 00:04:02,352
Maybe he's right.

114
00:04:02,551 --> 00:04:03,786
Mom, dad,

115
00:04:03,953 --> 00:04:06,163
I have done a lot
of driving practice,

116
00:04:06,279 --> 00:04:09,219
and I think I am finally ready
to take the next step.

117
00:04:09,332 --> 00:04:10,809
Finally. About time
you get out there and--

118
00:04:10,924 --> 00:04:12,192
Picking a keychain!

119
00:04:12,341 --> 00:04:13,627
(Keychains jangle)
Which one do you guys like?

120
00:04:13,752 --> 00:04:15,002
I've been collecting them
over the years,

121
00:04:15,133 --> 00:04:18,318
and now that I'm gonna drive,
it's finally time to choose.

122
00:04:18,470 --> 00:04:20,638
This one's "one direction."
"I 'heart' New York."

123
00:04:20,765 --> 00:04:22,814
I've got, like,
four "Brown County" ones.

124
00:04:22,973 --> 00:04:25,558
(Gasps) This one says
"I'm going commando."

125
00:04:25,684 --> 00:04:28,444
I don't really get it,
but I do support the military.

126
00:04:28,952 --> 00:04:29,770
(Sighs)

127
00:04:29,877 --> 00:04:31,239
Why don't you take the one
shaped like a key

128
00:04:31,364 --> 00:04:32,653
and put it in the ignition?

129
00:04:33,211 --> 00:04:34,748
I just want to be prepared.

130
00:04:34,891 --> 00:04:35,887
I'm not ready.

131
00:04:36,071 --> 00:04:39,225
I can't even narrow my keychains
down to a top three.

132
00:04:39,392 --> 00:04:41,870
Sue, you are ready.

133
00:04:42,006 --> 00:04:43,653
Remember when you didn't want
to take your training wheels

134
00:04:43,783 --> 00:04:45,327
off your bike, and we made you?

135
00:04:45,446 --> 00:04:46,511
What happened then?

136
00:04:46,634 --> 00:04:47,286
(Gasps)

137
00:04:47,390 --> 00:04:48,378
Oh, my God.

138
00:04:48,483 --> 00:04:52,420
This situation is very similar
to <i>that</i> situation.

139
00:04:53,036 --> 00:04:54,545
I <i>can</i> do this.

140
00:04:54,671 --> 00:04:57,791
(Gasps) I am gonna go
drive a car.

141
00:04:57,959 --> 00:04:59,132
(High-pitched voice)
Aah ha!

142
00:04:59,223 --> 00:05:00,508
(Normal voice)
I'll be waiting outside.

143
00:05:01,030 --> 00:05:02,399
(Keychains jangle, door opens)

144
00:05:02,974 --> 00:05:04,042
Oh, no.
(Door closes)

145
00:05:04,144 --> 00:05:06,402
You're the one that gave
the great speech. Get out there.

146
00:05:06,535 --> 00:05:07,793
Rock paper scissors?

147
00:05:10,658 --> 00:05:12,683
I worked the fish booth.
Have fun.

148
00:05:13,051 --> 00:05:13,818
(Grunts)

149
00:05:21,401 --> 00:05:22,843
I thought mom
was coming with me.

150
00:05:22,984 --> 00:05:24,794
Well, we rock-paper-scissored
for it.

151
00:05:24,901 --> 00:05:26,059
And you won?

152
00:05:26,284 --> 00:05:27,841
Sure.
Let's go with that.

153
00:05:28,056 --> 00:05:29,286
Okay. Start her up.
(Seat belt clicks)

154
00:05:29,426 --> 00:05:30,283
(Exhales deeply)

155
00:05:31,439 --> 00:05:32,233
(Engine starts)

156
00:05:32,340 --> 00:05:33,462
Aah!

157
00:05:33,954 --> 00:05:35,291
Okay. Now put it
in reverse.

158
00:05:35,394 --> 00:05:37,887
Dad, hold on. I have to
go through my checklist first.

159
00:05:38,912 --> 00:05:40,761
Mirrors... check.

160
00:05:40,964 --> 00:05:41,759
Signal...

161
00:05:41,876 --> 00:05:43,002
(Click) Check.

162
00:05:43,363 --> 00:05:44,591
(Click) Wipers...

163
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,122
(Whirs)

164
00:05:46,513 --> 00:05:47,552
Check.

165
00:05:47,665 --> 00:05:48,850
How are the weather conditions?

166
00:05:49,631 --> 00:05:51,052
We're not flying
cross-country.

167
00:05:51,165 --> 00:05:52,148
We're going around the block.

168
00:05:52,245 --> 00:05:53,431
This is my process.

169
00:05:54,677 --> 00:05:56,796
Hands at 10:00 and 2:00...
Check.

170
00:05:57,019 --> 00:05:57,889
(Exhales)

171
00:05:58,126 --> 00:06:01,280
Dad, I saw that.
You're making me nervous.

172
00:06:01,388 --> 00:06:02,956
I don't want you
looking at me. Look away.

173
00:06:03,151 --> 00:06:03,951
What?

174
00:06:04,061 --> 00:06:05,308
Look away.

175
00:06:07,634 --> 00:06:09,163
Is the brake
in the right position?

176
00:06:09,343 --> 00:06:11,326
How am I supposed to tell
when I'm looking away?

177
00:06:11,453 --> 00:06:13,441
Okay, you can look,
and then look away.

178
00:06:13,535 --> 00:06:14,472
Okay, Sue, this is nuts.

179
00:06:14,580 --> 00:06:15,806
You do realize
when you're out on the road,

180
00:06:15,913 --> 00:06:17,366
other drivers
are gonna be watching you?

181
00:06:17,496 --> 00:06:19,688
That's the deal with driving.
Everybody looks at each other.

182
00:06:19,859 --> 00:06:22,685
I just want to be prepared for
every single possible situation.

183
00:06:22,802 --> 00:06:24,659
There's a million unpredictable
things that can happen.

184
00:06:24,882 --> 00:06:26,279
Well, now you're
making me scared.

185
00:06:26,382 --> 00:06:28,450
Well, don't be. When you drive,
you have to be confident.

186
00:06:28,554 --> 00:06:30,500
You can't just tell someone
to <i>be</i> confident!

187
00:06:30,597 --> 00:06:32,418
Okay, enough. Let's go.
You're gonna run out of gas.

188
00:06:32,531 --> 00:06:34,148
Okay, let me just run
through my checklist first.

189
00:06:34,267 --> 00:06:35,138
No, no more checklists.

190
00:06:35,232 --> 00:06:37,047
Just go. Come on.
Pull out now. Pull out.

191
00:06:37,155 --> 00:06:37,779
(Gears grind)

192
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:38,968
- What the hell are you doing?!
- Aah!

193
00:06:39,083 --> 00:06:40,030
The car's already going!

194
00:06:40,156 --> 00:06:41,562
I'm s-- it's--
I just thought--

195
00:06:41,742 --> 00:06:43,963
(Crying) - Aah!
- Okay-- mm.

196
00:06:44,092 --> 00:06:45,890
I'm never driving
with you again!

197
00:06:47,118 --> 00:06:48,791
Wha--
(Seat belt whirs)

198
00:06:52,883 --> 00:06:53,807
(Door closes)

199
00:06:54,543 --> 00:06:56,661
<i>So the next day,</i>
<i>we tried it again</i>

200
00:06:56,773 --> 00:06:58,435
<i>with a gentler approach.</i>

201
00:06:59,013 --> 00:07:00,451
Can I go over my checklist?
(Seat belt clicks)

202
00:07:00,575 --> 00:07:02,816
Sure, honey,
that's a great idea.

203
00:07:02,931 --> 00:07:04,854
Whatever makes you comfortable.

204
00:07:05,377 --> 00:07:07,456
Brakes... check.

205
00:07:08,192 --> 00:07:09,283
Mirrors...

206
00:07:09,497 --> 00:07:10,447
Check.

207
00:07:10,707 --> 00:07:11,787
Signals...
(Click)

208
00:07:11,968 --> 00:07:12,924
Check.

209
00:07:13,048 --> 00:07:14,661
This is gonna be fun, huh?

210
00:07:14,810 --> 00:07:17,772
A couple of chicks out driving
like "Thelma & Louise."

211
00:07:17,985 --> 00:07:20,396
I mean the beginning
of that movie, but...

212
00:07:20,749 --> 00:07:22,788
You know what?
Don't see it.

213
00:07:22,992 --> 00:07:25,298
All right, then.
Here we go.

214
00:07:25,604 --> 00:07:27,329
Why don't you start the car?

215
00:07:29,857 --> 00:07:31,330
(Engine starts)

216
00:07:32,132 --> 00:07:33,322
(Exhales deeply)

217
00:07:33,467 --> 00:07:35,537
Now you're gonna want
to shift into reverse.

218
00:07:35,662 --> 00:07:37,567
Stop rushing me!

219
00:07:37,758 --> 00:07:39,246
(Crying) Oh, my God!

220
00:07:39,369 --> 00:07:40,885
You're worse than dad!
(Gasps)

221
00:07:41,022 --> 00:07:42,413
Honey.
(Door thuds)

222
00:07:43,089 --> 00:07:44,170
(Seat belt clicks) Ugh!

223
00:07:44,372 --> 00:07:45,711
(Cries) Honey!

224
00:07:46,276 --> 00:07:47,207
Ugh.
(Door closes)

225
00:07:55,143 --> 00:07:56,116
(Doorbell rings)

226
00:07:56,233 --> 00:07:58,021
<i>So I couldn't teach</i>
<i>my daughter to drive,</i>

227
00:07:58,194 --> 00:08:01,063
<i>and I let my neighbor take</i>
<i>my son trick-or-treating.</i>

228
00:08:01,513 --> 00:08:03,649
<i>But Halloween</i>
<i>wasn't a complete bust.</i>

229
00:08:03,766 --> 00:08:05,008
(Children, singsong voices)
Trick or treat!

230
00:08:05,198 --> 00:08:06,527
There you go.

231
00:08:06,988 --> 00:08:07,840
Thanks.

232
00:08:08,069 --> 00:08:09,680
Yeah. Thanks.

233
00:08:09,928 --> 00:08:10,751
(Mouths words)

234
00:08:16,710 --> 00:08:17,904
(Sighs)

235
00:08:18,666 --> 00:08:19,824
(Door opens)

236
00:08:19,940 --> 00:08:20,898
Hey, mom.

237
00:08:21,014 --> 00:08:21,836
(High-pitched voice)
Whoop.

238
00:08:21,935 --> 00:08:23,978
Hey, Brick.
You're back already, huh?

239
00:08:24,107 --> 00:08:25,043
How was it?

240
00:08:25,235 --> 00:08:26,037
Awesome.

241
00:08:26,146 --> 00:08:28,304
Mrs. Donahue brought
thermoses of apple cider,

242
00:08:28,447 --> 00:08:30,452
and then she took us
to Orson Heights.

243
00:08:30,568 --> 00:08:32,521
Everyone was giving out
full-sized candy bars,

244
00:08:32,645 --> 00:08:33,842
and the houses are huge.

245
00:08:34,001 --> 00:08:35,703
Have you ever considered
moving there?

246
00:08:35,852 --> 00:08:37,253
Come on. Unload the loot.

247
00:08:37,386 --> 00:08:39,340
Mama's jonesing for a Kit Kat.

248
00:08:40,098 --> 00:08:41,071
<i>(TV playing indistinctly)</i>

249
00:08:44,235 --> 00:08:45,317
Whoa.

250
00:08:45,861 --> 00:08:49,619
Brick, that is
a buttload of candy.

251
00:08:49,732 --> 00:08:50,700
I know.

252
00:08:50,842 --> 00:08:52,060
By my calculations,

253
00:08:52,212 --> 00:08:54,182
I should have enough
to eat a piece every day

254
00:08:54,303 --> 00:08:55,892
for the next year and a half.

255
00:08:55,998 --> 00:08:59,695
(Mouth full) Oh, but you are not
eating all this candy.

256
00:08:59,895 --> 00:09:01,606
Okay, tell you what--
we'll make a deal.

257
00:09:01,738 --> 00:09:03,035
You can eat as much as you want

258
00:09:03,155 --> 00:09:04,366
for the next 24 hours,

259
00:09:04,533 --> 00:09:07,205
and then we're sending the rest
to the soldiers overseas.

260
00:09:07,323 --> 00:09:09,088
- Hmm?
(Exhales) - Fine.

261
00:09:09,197 --> 00:09:10,833
All right? Come on.
Time for bed.

262
00:09:11,451 --> 00:09:12,519
(Dog barks in distance)

263
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:21,969
<i>So another Halloween</i>
<i>had come and gone,</i>

264
00:09:22,167 --> 00:09:24,299
<i>and I, for one, was relieved.</i>

265
00:09:24,486 --> 00:09:26,913
Mom, I did it.
I completed your challenge.

266
00:09:27,079 --> 00:09:28,809
Challenge? What challenge?

267
00:09:28,950 --> 00:09:30,539
I ate all my candy in 24 hours,

268
00:09:30,658 --> 00:09:31,722
just like you said.

269
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:40,922
You told him to eat
all his candy?

270
00:09:41,042 --> 00:09:41,811
No!

271
00:09:41,918 --> 00:09:42,944
You said I had to finish it.

272
00:09:43,077 --> 00:09:44,597
No, I didn't!

273
00:09:44,843 --> 00:09:48,212
(Scoffs) I thought he would
eat some, get sick,

274
00:09:48,328 --> 00:09:49,564
and not want the rest.

275
00:09:49,689 --> 00:09:51,561
You know, like when
someone starts smoking,

276
00:09:51,686 --> 00:09:54,591
and you-- you force them to smoke
an entire carton of cigarettes.

277
00:09:54,724 --> 00:09:56,562
Not really helping your case
for mother of the year.

278
00:09:56,752 --> 00:09:57,448
(Sighs)

279
00:09:58,087 --> 00:09:59,848
How in the world
could you possibly

280
00:09:59,971 --> 00:10:01,305
have eaten all that candy?

281
00:10:08,733 --> 00:10:10,453
(Whirring)

282
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:18,251
It wasn't easy,
but I powered through.

283
00:10:18,373 --> 00:10:20,122
There's nothing left?

284
00:10:20,243 --> 00:10:21,932
Not even a tootsie roll?

285
00:10:22,098 --> 00:10:23,583
You know, for the soldiers.

286
00:10:23,763 --> 00:10:25,264
I'm actually
not feeling too well.

287
00:10:25,446 --> 00:10:26,825
If I still feel
like this tomorrow,

288
00:10:26,944 --> 00:10:28,255
can I stay home from school?

289
00:10:28,406 --> 00:10:29,461
(Scoffs)
You're not skipping school

290
00:10:29,585 --> 00:10:31,427
'cause your mom made you eat
a ton of candy.

291
00:10:31,549 --> 00:10:33,865
And don't you dare
say that at school.

292
00:10:33,983 --> 00:10:35,419
We're already in the system.

293
00:10:36,337 --> 00:10:37,150
Come on, mom.

294
00:10:37,265 --> 00:10:38,764
I'm leaving
the driveway this time.

295
00:10:38,867 --> 00:10:39,890
I can feel it.

296
00:10:40,663 --> 00:10:41,828
(Sighs) (Sighs)

297
00:10:48,683 --> 00:10:50,244
- What's this?
- Check it out.

298
00:10:50,980 --> 00:10:52,744
This guy's running
for city council.

299
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:55,063
His name's Harry Butts.

300
00:10:55,220 --> 00:10:57,571
(Laughs) Like, seriously.
It's his real name.

301
00:10:58,018 --> 00:10:59,948
How could we not
put this sign up? Right?

302
00:11:00,061 --> 00:11:01,519
I mean you get why
that's funny, right, dad?

303
00:11:01,656 --> 00:11:03,303
(Car engine starts) Yeah, I
think I can crack that code.

304
00:11:03,448 --> 00:11:04,459
(Sue) I am calm...

305
00:11:05,595 --> 00:11:07,443
confident, and in control.
(Snickers)

306
00:11:07,564 --> 00:11:08,637
I am ready!

307
00:11:09,006 --> 00:11:10,038
I am not ready.

308
00:11:10,422 --> 00:11:11,113
What's the holdup?

309
00:11:11,218 --> 00:11:12,528
She says she's not ready.

310
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:14,238
Come on, Sue. You can do it.
Just go.

311
00:11:14,309 --> 00:11:15,967
I will. I just need
to do my checklist first.

312
00:11:16,088 --> 00:11:17,774
- Go!
- Oh, stop it, Axl!

313
00:11:17,903 --> 00:11:18,630
Honey, come on.

314
00:11:18,750 --> 00:11:19,955
- I will. I will.
- All right.

315
00:11:20,077 --> 00:11:22,251
- Just put it in gear.
(Mike) - Come on.

316
00:11:22,681 --> 00:11:25,403
- If you just do it, it's gonna get
easier every time. - This is annoying!

317
00:11:25,532 --> 00:11:26,600
- Okay!
- There you go.

318
00:11:26,725 --> 00:11:27,619
That's it. Ease out.
(Crunch)

319
00:11:27,740 --> 00:11:29,314
- Aah!
- Hey, hey, hey! You're on his foot!

320
00:11:29,421 --> 00:11:30,176
- Aah!
- Back up!

321
00:11:30,293 --> 00:11:31,223
Stop! Stop! Stop!

322
00:11:31,331 --> 00:11:32,450
Put it in gear!
Keep going! Back up!

323
00:11:32,555 --> 00:11:33,604
Move it forward!
What are you doing?!

324
00:11:33,715 --> 00:11:35,741
- Go, go, go, go, go!
- Is it "stop" or is it "go"?

325
00:11:35,850 --> 00:11:37,446
- Go forward! Go one way or the other!
- Move! Move!

326
00:11:37,579 --> 00:11:39,339
- You're on his foot!
- Go! Get it off of my foot!

327
00:11:39,454 --> 00:11:40,918
Just let me do
my checklist! Oh!

328
00:11:41,042 --> 00:11:42,324
(Frankie) - Sue, just get out.
- Come here.

329
00:11:42,459 --> 00:11:43,828
(Axl) My foot! Sue!
(Sue crying)

330
00:11:43,983 --> 00:11:44,845
- Aah!
- Oh, my God! Hurry up!

331
00:11:44,973 --> 00:11:46,897
Oh! Oh.

332
00:11:47,449 --> 00:11:49,296
Oh. Aah.

333
00:11:49,413 --> 00:11:52,049
(Crying) I told you
I wasn't ready.

334
00:12:03,569 --> 00:12:05,305
Person on crutches
coming through.

335
00:12:05,450 --> 00:12:06,751
Oh, does it hurt?

336
00:12:06,882 --> 00:12:08,774
Let's see.
I had a car on my foot.

337
00:12:08,874 --> 00:12:10,094
Yeah. It hurts.

338
00:12:10,856 --> 00:12:12,667
Is he gonna be able
to play football?

339
00:12:12,802 --> 00:12:15,060
Not for a while.
Lucky it's just a sprain.

340
00:12:15,168 --> 00:12:16,132
Doctors said
if he would have broken it,

341
00:12:16,250 --> 00:12:17,532
he'd have been out
for the rest of the season.

342
00:12:17,645 --> 00:12:19,078
Which would have meant
good-bye, scholarship.

343
00:12:19,183 --> 00:12:20,097
Ugh.

344
00:12:20,473 --> 00:12:21,583
Hey, Axl,

345
00:12:21,989 --> 00:12:23,272
I just wanted to say...

346
00:12:23,403 --> 00:12:24,311
Get her out!

347
00:12:25,342 --> 00:12:27,211
I just wanted to say
I am so stupid.

348
00:12:27,313 --> 00:12:28,619
Get her out!
(Thud)

349
00:12:29,809 --> 00:12:31,829
- Oh.
- What?

350
00:12:32,669 --> 00:12:35,114
<i>I'd been dreading the fallout</i>
<i>from Brick's candy binge,</i>

351
00:12:35,255 --> 00:12:38,145
<i>and as sure as you can say</i>
<i>"creamy nougat caramel center,"</i>

352
00:12:38,337 --> 00:12:39,505
<i>the call came.</i>
(Beep)

353
00:12:39,616 --> 00:12:40,899
Well, that was the school.

354
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:42,922
Brick's teacher
wants to see us.

355
00:12:43,044 --> 00:12:44,343
(Sighs) Great.

356
00:12:44,481 --> 00:12:46,598
I forced him to go to school
after Halloween,

357
00:12:46,717 --> 00:12:47,705
and he probably threw up

358
00:12:47,827 --> 00:12:49,776
and told everyone I made him
eat all his candy.

359
00:12:49,984 --> 00:12:51,622
(Axl) I'm out of chips!
(Clicks)

360
00:12:51,734 --> 00:12:53,271
Not now, Axl!

361
00:12:53,397 --> 00:12:55,246
Oh, God, and we'd made it
all the way to November

362
00:12:55,366 --> 00:12:56,977
without getting a call
from Brick's teacher.

363
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,351
That was a new record for us.

364
00:12:58,479 --> 00:13:00,374
(Singsongy) Hello! Chips!

365
00:13:00,487 --> 00:13:02,272
Well, someone's
gonna have to go down there.

366
00:13:02,437 --> 00:13:05,094
<i>Somebody?</i> You're the one
who challenged Brick

367
00:13:05,222 --> 00:13:06,483
to eat 20 pounds of candy.

368
00:13:06,627 --> 00:13:08,094
It wasn't a challenge.

369
00:13:08,210 --> 00:13:09,557
Chips!
(Clanging)

370
00:13:10,729 --> 00:13:11,721
Okay.

371
00:13:12,260 --> 00:13:13,698
One, two...

372
00:13:13,833 --> 00:13:15,158
Fine. I'm going.

373
00:13:18,895 --> 00:13:22,676
You probably have an idea
of why I called you in.

374
00:13:22,875 --> 00:13:24,153
I might.

375
00:13:24,284 --> 00:13:27,808
You see, Brick came in
the day after Halloween--

376
00:13:27,928 --> 00:13:28,953
Okay, I don't know
what he told you,

377
00:13:29,063 --> 00:13:29,895
but I can explain.

378
00:13:30,033 --> 00:13:31,577
I wasn't even there.
Somebody else took him.

379
00:13:31,696 --> 00:13:33,015
Gave him
this huge pillowcase--

380
00:13:33,137 --> 00:13:35,012
He's been <i>great.</i>

381
00:13:35,230 --> 00:13:37,360
What? He has?

382
00:13:37,514 --> 00:13:39,737
Let me tell you
a little about myself.

383
00:13:39,839 --> 00:13:44,436
I am the type of person
who likes things a certain way.

384
00:13:44,597 --> 00:13:49,234
I have no use
for outside-the-box thinking.

385
00:13:49,435 --> 00:13:50,838
Needless to say,

386
00:13:51,169 --> 00:13:54,349
I have not been
a big fan of Brick.

387
00:13:54,477 --> 00:13:57,021
Yeah, he's pretty far
outside that box.

388
00:13:57,158 --> 00:14:00,102
But since the day
after Halloween,

389
00:14:00,283 --> 00:14:02,635
Brick has been a <i>dream.</i>

390
00:14:02,807 --> 00:14:06,599
All his whispering
and whooping gone.

391
00:14:06,795 --> 00:14:07,886
(Laughs) Wow.

392
00:14:08,099 --> 00:14:09,625
You know, when you
called me in here,

393
00:14:09,763 --> 00:14:10,824
I thought...

394
00:14:11,536 --> 00:14:13,341
You know what?
I interrupted you.

395
00:14:13,462 --> 00:14:14,364
Go on.

396
00:14:14,505 --> 00:14:18,401
Has Brick been put
on any medication recently?

397
00:14:18,735 --> 00:14:21,135
Sort... of?

398
00:14:21,271 --> 00:14:23,694
Don't need to know.
Just more paperwork.

399
00:14:23,828 --> 00:14:27,337
The point is,
whatever you're doing,

400
00:14:27,878 --> 00:14:29,070
keep it up.

401
00:14:31,201 --> 00:14:33,084
Okay, here's what
I'm thinking--

402
00:14:33,245 --> 00:14:35,538
a cupcake for breakfast,
twinkies for lunch,

403
00:14:35,702 --> 00:14:36,611
and we sneak some M&M's

404
00:14:36,755 --> 00:14:38,213
into his hamburger meat
at dinner.

405
00:14:38,542 --> 00:14:40,419
He's not a dog, Frankie.
(Door opens and closes)

406
00:14:41,915 --> 00:14:44,724
Hi, mom. Hi, dad.
How was work today, dad?

407
00:14:44,985 --> 00:14:47,048
Uh... fine.

408
00:14:47,884 --> 00:14:50,370
Would you like to hear
about my day? It was great.

409
00:14:50,486 --> 00:14:52,505
I played some four square
with some kids at recess,

410
00:14:52,632 --> 00:14:54,422
and then we shot
some hoops after school.

411
00:14:54,889 --> 00:14:56,556
Anyways, I'm gonna
go pick up my room now.

412
00:14:56,685 --> 00:14:58,865
If you guys wanna do
anything later, let me know.

413
00:15:01,490 --> 00:15:03,740
Wouldn't want to leave this out
where someone could trip on it.

414
00:15:04,656 --> 00:15:06,118
(Dog barks in distance)

415
00:15:07,130 --> 00:15:08,484
That kid has
a year and a half of candy

416
00:15:08,611 --> 00:15:11,176
- coursing through his veins.
- He's more sugar than boy.

417
00:15:11,301 --> 00:15:13,201
But it's made him... normal.

418
00:15:13,389 --> 00:15:16,869
I'm telling you, we have
stumbled onto something here.

419
00:15:16,990 --> 00:15:20,117
It's like "Lorenzo's oil."
People should know about this.

420
00:15:20,257 --> 00:15:22,836
Frankie, nobody <i>ever</i>
needs to know about this.

421
00:15:23,490 --> 00:15:24,511
(Sighs)

422
00:15:32,136 --> 00:15:33,476
<i>Brick might have been</i>
<i>on a high,</i>

423
00:15:33,604 --> 00:15:35,190
<i>but Sue was on a low.</i>

424
00:15:35,326 --> 00:15:38,347
<i>With one disastrous car ride,</i>
<i>Sue managed to not only put</i>

425
00:15:38,515 --> 00:15:40,298
<i>Axl's football career</i>
<i>in jeopardy,</i>

426
00:15:40,450 --> 00:15:42,691
<i>but also Orson High's</i>
<i>perfect record.</i>

427
00:15:43,494 --> 00:15:45,570
(Crowd shouting indistinctly,
whistle blows)

428
00:15:45,755 --> 00:15:47,858
<i>(Man over PA)</i>
<i>Touchdown, warriors.</i>

429
00:15:48,808 --> 00:15:50,087
You know who would have
stopped that guy?

430
00:15:50,235 --> 00:15:52,165
- Axl.
- Yeah, he would have.

431
00:15:52,319 --> 00:15:54,865
I can't believe his stupid
sister ran over his foot.

432
00:15:54,997 --> 00:15:56,327
I didn't even know
he had a sister.

433
00:15:56,442 --> 00:15:57,979
How do you even
run over someone's foot?

434
00:15:58,138 --> 00:16:00,710
If we lose this game tonight,
it is all her fault!

435
00:16:01,254 --> 00:16:03,409
This is the worst thing
that's ever happened.

436
00:16:03,544 --> 00:16:04,584
- I know!
- Totally!

437
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:06,480
This doesn't just
ruin his life!

438
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:07,919
Now she ruined
the whole school!

439
00:16:08,900 --> 00:16:11,692
(REM's "Everybody Hurts" playing)

440
00:16:11,833 --> 00:16:16,085
♪ And everybody hurts ♪

441
00:16:16,818 --> 00:16:20,534
♪ sometimes ♪

442
00:16:23,488 --> 00:16:26,624
♪ sometimes everything is wrong ♪
(Electricity crackles)

443
00:16:31,763 --> 00:16:34,627
♪ Now it's time to sing along ♪

444
00:16:34,750 --> 00:16:38,574
♪ when your day is night alone ♪
♪ hold on ♪

445
00:16:39,987 --> 00:16:41,149
(Bottles clink)

446
00:16:44,543 --> 00:16:45,820
Hey, Axl.

447
00:16:48,528 --> 00:16:49,876
Bologna, huh?

448
00:16:50,238 --> 00:16:51,718
That's a great choice.
(Clatter)

449
00:16:52,467 --> 00:16:54,128
Hey, you know,
I can carry that stuff.

450
00:16:54,324 --> 00:16:55,441
It'd be no problem.

451
00:16:55,593 --> 00:16:56,686
Haven't you done
enough already?

452
00:16:56,804 --> 00:16:58,020
First, you knock me
out of football,

453
00:16:58,147 --> 00:17:01,387
now you gotta brag about
how you're able to carry stuff?

454
00:17:01,828 --> 00:17:02,407
No.

455
00:17:02,536 --> 00:17:04,615
I mean, I can carry it <i>for you.</i>

456
00:17:05,344 --> 00:17:06,275
Oh.

457
00:17:06,578 --> 00:17:07,430
Look, Axl,

458
00:17:07,623 --> 00:17:09,064
I know how much
football means to you,

459
00:17:09,180 --> 00:17:11,499
and I would never do
<i>anything</i> to ruin that,

460
00:17:11,616 --> 00:17:13,306
or your chance of getting
a college scholarship.

461
00:17:13,452 --> 00:17:16,412
I am <i>so</i> very sorry,

462
00:17:16,569 --> 00:17:19,419
very, very, very sorry
for spraining your foot.

463
00:17:19,553 --> 00:17:20,668
I mean, if I could go back

464
00:17:20,803 --> 00:17:22,883
a-and run over
my own foot with the car,

465
00:17:23,019 --> 00:17:24,777
I would, but I don't think
it's physically possible

466
00:17:24,914 --> 00:17:26,192
to do that
from the driver's seat.

467
00:17:26,309 --> 00:17:27,993
Well, if anyone
could do it, you could.

468
00:17:32,016 --> 00:17:34,295
Wait. Did you vote
for Harry Butts today?

469
00:17:34,596 --> 00:17:36,017
No, I'm gonna do it tomorrow.

470
00:17:36,514 --> 00:17:38,696
But today is election day.

471
00:17:39,441 --> 00:17:40,680
It's only one day?

472
00:17:41,728 --> 00:17:42,753
Damn it!

473
00:17:43,231 --> 00:17:44,874
How am I supposed to
get to the election place?

474
00:17:44,982 --> 00:17:46,552
I can't drive,
and nobody's home!

475
00:17:48,768 --> 00:17:50,286
(Under breath) Oh.

476
00:17:52,362 --> 00:17:54,223
(Normal voice)
Fine. You can take me.

477
00:17:54,354 --> 00:17:56,132
What?! I can't do that!

478
00:17:56,261 --> 00:17:58,295
- Hey, you owe me this.
- But I can't.

479
00:17:58,464 --> 00:18:00,760
I am a danger to everyone
on the road...

480
00:18:00,889 --> 00:18:02,127
even near the road.

481
00:18:02,251 --> 00:18:03,683
Look, this is important.

482
00:18:03,852 --> 00:18:05,657
My whole life, people have been
telling me what to do--

483
00:18:05,808 --> 00:18:08,072
"Sit up straight!"
"That cup's not a toilet!"

484
00:18:08,211 --> 00:18:09,163
"Clean your room!"

485
00:18:09,282 --> 00:18:11,326
Well, now I finally have a say.

486
00:18:11,462 --> 00:18:12,493
Now...

487
00:18:12,799 --> 00:18:14,914
I get to tell America
to clean its room.

488
00:18:15,117 --> 00:18:15,779
(Slaps pamphlet on table)

489
00:18:15,909 --> 00:18:18,414
But I'm scared.
What if I mess up again?

490
00:18:18,550 --> 00:18:21,439
Sue, let me tell you
why I'm so awesome.

491
00:18:21,629 --> 00:18:24,240
You see, even when I have
no idea what I'm doing,

492
00:18:24,370 --> 00:18:26,817
I pretend I do. That's why
I'm good at everything.

493
00:18:26,986 --> 00:18:29,861
This guy Harry Butts--
He should be living in a hole.

494
00:18:29,987 --> 00:18:30,679
But he has the guts

495
00:18:30,777 --> 00:18:32,338
to put his name on signs
all over town

496
00:18:32,469 --> 00:18:33,996
and run for office.
If he can do that,

497
00:18:34,155 --> 00:18:35,807
then you gotta step it up
and get me there

498
00:18:35,957 --> 00:18:37,178
so I can vote for him.

499
00:18:37,728 --> 00:18:39,239
Do it for America!

500
00:18:39,381 --> 00:18:41,003
I just love America so much.

501
00:18:42,149 --> 00:18:43,595
I'll do it!

502
00:18:44,741 --> 00:18:46,537
But wait--
I need an adult in the car.

503
00:18:47,302 --> 00:18:49,323
Voting is a big responsibility.

504
00:18:49,454 --> 00:18:51,481
That's why
I'm voting for Truman.

505
00:18:52,317 --> 00:18:53,799
I'm driving!

506
00:18:53,936 --> 00:18:55,973
Oh, good, then I'm not.

507
00:18:56,446 --> 00:18:57,773
(Liquid sloshes)

508
00:19:00,971 --> 00:19:03,437
So Mr. Walker was teaching
a lesson on fractions

509
00:19:03,616 --> 00:19:06,117
and stopped to ask
if everyone understood.

510
00:19:06,463 --> 00:19:07,790
And then I said,

511
00:19:08,053 --> 00:19:10,482
"I think we get about 3/4
of what you're saying,

512
00:19:10,623 --> 00:19:12,567
maybe 7/8."
(Frankie and Mike laugh)

513
00:19:13,306 --> 00:19:15,473
Yeah, everyone had
a good laugh at that one,

514
00:19:15,603 --> 00:19:16,931
even Mr. Walker.

515
00:19:17,100 --> 00:19:18,805
Oh, can I take
your plates to the kitchen?

516
00:19:19,386 --> 00:19:20,890
- Oh, uh, sure.
- Sure.

517
00:19:24,975 --> 00:19:27,788
Wow. He's great, isn't he?

518
00:19:27,907 --> 00:19:29,917
I know.
(Water running in faucet)

519
00:19:30,024 --> 00:19:30,866
It's weird, though, right?

520
00:19:30,989 --> 00:19:32,252
Oh, my God. It's so weird.

521
00:19:32,396 --> 00:19:33,688
I mean, he's engaged
and connecting,

522
00:19:33,814 --> 00:19:36,431
but without his quirks,
he's just not Brick.

523
00:19:36,724 --> 00:19:38,544
Oh, one more thing.

524
00:19:38,682 --> 00:19:39,972
There's a permission slip
in the--

525
00:19:40,426 --> 00:19:41,934
(Thud)

526
00:19:45,244 --> 00:19:47,423
Hey, buddy. You okay?

527
00:19:48,152 --> 00:19:49,926
Can someone bring me a book?

528
00:19:51,563 --> 00:19:54,629
Brick, you said something
about a permission slip?

529
00:19:56,173 --> 00:19:58,028
If people are allergic to bees,

530
00:19:58,165 --> 00:20:00,258
can bees be allergic to people?

531
00:20:00,412 --> 00:20:01,543
(High-pitched voice)
Whoop!

532
00:20:03,393 --> 00:20:05,037
Maybe we can give him
a little sugar,

533
00:20:05,164 --> 00:20:06,552
on special occasions.

534
00:20:06,687 --> 00:20:08,717
Like SATs
or college interviews?

535
00:20:08,872 --> 00:20:10,556
- School dances?
- Oh, that's a good one.

536
00:20:11,336 --> 00:20:13,100
(Indistinct conversations)

537
00:20:13,217 --> 00:20:14,873
Where's the girl
with the bathing suits

538
00:20:14,996 --> 00:20:16,828
I wanted to try on?

539
00:20:17,023 --> 00:20:17,821
(Curtain swishes)

540
00:20:17,934 --> 00:20:19,423
Democracy rules!

541
00:20:19,871 --> 00:20:20,970
Give me my sticker.

542
00:20:21,390 --> 00:20:23,720
<i>But the most important vote</i>
<i>that Axl cast that day</i>

543
00:20:23,847 --> 00:20:26,434
<i>was the vote of confidence</i>
<i>in his sister.</i>

544
00:20:26,638 --> 00:20:28,223
I did my checklist
while you were voting,

545
00:20:28,362 --> 00:20:29,923
so we are ready to roll.

546
00:20:30,430 --> 00:20:31,121
(Chuckles)

547
00:20:31,227 --> 00:20:32,141
Here.

548
00:20:32,401 --> 00:20:34,179
<i>So Axl had forgiven Sue...</i>

549
00:20:34,430 --> 00:20:35,322
<i>sort of.</i>

550
00:20:35,479 --> 00:20:36,952
<i>And sugar-free Brick</i>
<i>was a lot more</i>

551
00:20:37,063 --> 00:20:38,492
<i>like the one we were used to.</i>

552
00:20:38,622 --> 00:20:39,964
<i>Yep, it looked like things</i>

553
00:20:40,099 --> 00:20:41,958
<i>might just be</i>
<i>getting back to normal.</i>

554
00:20:42,462 --> 00:20:44,445
(Telephone ringing)

555
00:20:44,549 --> 00:20:45,743
Brick?

556
00:20:46,059 --> 00:20:47,148
You gonna get the...

557
00:20:47,295 --> 00:20:48,047
(Ring)

558
00:20:48,144 --> 00:20:50,094
Never mind.
(Beeps)

559
00:20:50,375 --> 00:20:51,583
Hello?

560
00:20:51,813 --> 00:20:53,503
Yeah, this is Axl's mom.

561
00:20:55,188 --> 00:20:57,561
Oh. Uh-huh?

562
00:20:58,404 --> 00:21:00,231
Oh, no. Really?

563
00:21:01,016 --> 00:21:02,076
It's the doctor.

564
00:21:02,211 --> 00:21:03,623
He showed the film
to a specialist.

565
00:21:03,742 --> 00:21:05,343
Axl's foot isn't sprained.

566
00:21:06,121 --> 00:21:07,256
It's broken.

567
00:21:07,753 --> 00:21:08,776
<i>Like I said...</i>

568
00:21:08,933 --> 00:21:10,218
<i>(Thunderclap)</i>

569
00:21:10,344 --> 00:21:12,370
<i>It's a scary time of year.</i>

570
00:21:12,475 --> 00:21:14,662
(Axl) Aah!

571
00:21:15,930 --> 00:21:20,514
Sync and corrections by n17t01
www.addic7ed.com

